@startuml workflow
title Recovery code backup and use
footer (C)2026 Sean Donnellan
skinparam Shadowing 1
skinparam BackgroundColor #fff/aaf
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fff/aaf
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #fff-aaf
hide footbox

actor User
participant "Rust CLI" as CLI
participant "Phone: QRbot / NFC Tools" as Phone
participant "Wooden NTAG215 card" as Card
participant "Opaque RF-shielded holder" as Holder
participant Service

User -> Service: Save recovery codes
activate Service
deactivate Service
User -> CLI: Select tag and codes file
activate CLI
User -> CLI: Enter instructions or select instructions file
note over CLI, Phone
Keep passwords out of this workflow.
Files, app history, sync, and clipboards can retain codes.
A leak must not reveal both login factors.
end note
CLI -> CLI: Check text plus NDEF storage

alt Too large
    CLI --> User: Shorten instructions; no output
else Fits tag
    CLI --> User: Private text, A4 PDF, SVG and PNG files
    deactivate CLI
    User -> Phone: Scan QR; view full text
    activate Phone
    deactivate Phone
    User -> User: Compare codes and instructions
    User -> User: Print A4 PDF at actual size; check text and QR
    note over User, Holder
Store the paper backup separately under lock.
Print and laser jobs can retain plaintext.
Anyone with the opened card can copy its codes.
end note
    User -> Phone: Paste payload as one English Text record
    activate Phone
    Phone -> Card: Write NFC
    activate Card
    Card --> Phone: Read full text back
    deactivate Card
    deactivate Phone
    note over Phone, Card
No tag read password or payload encryption by choice.
Optional NFC read protection cannot protect the QR.
Encryption adds a recovery secret and a decrypting step.
end note
    User -> User: Compare payload; engrave cover; fit inlay
    User -> Phone: Scan finished QR and read NFC
    activate Phone
    deactivate Phone
    User -> Holder: Store card
    User -> Phone: remove temporary copies
    activate Phone
    deactivate Phone
end

group Recovery after successful backup
    note over User, Holder
If the card is unavailable, use the separate paper backup.
After loss or suspected copying, replace the code set
and every backup. A spare copy does not revoke a lost one.
end note
    User -> Holder: Remove card
    activate Phone
    alt NFC
        Phone -> Card: Read with NFC Tools
        activate Card
        Card --> Phone: Codes and instructions
        deactivate Card
    else QR
        User -> Phone: Scan with QRbot; view text
    end
    Phone --> User: Display codes and instructions
    deactivate Phone
    User -> Service: Follow instructions; use one unused code
    activate Service
    deactivate Service
    User -> User: Mark code spent with marker; clear temporary copies; store card
end
@enduml